    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **269 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp08Tests` and all existing owner/repository tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented owner `registrationDate` defaulting to today's date, returned in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `Owner` schema, which generates a `LocalDate registrationDate` on `OwnerDto`. It's on `Owner` (not `OwnerFields`), so it's response-only, never accepted as input.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\", columnDefinition = \"DATE\")`) with getter/setter, mirroring how `Pet.birthDate` is modeled.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so this is what lets the value round-trip through the DB on the follow-up GET.\n\n4. **`function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 After mapping the request into an `Owner`, set `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null. Since the input DTO never carries the field, every created owner gets today's date.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically (same name/type on both `Owner` and `OwnerDto`), and Jackson serializes `LocalDate` as an ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string \u2014 matching the test's `today()` expectation.",
